[2.918, "o", "\u001b[1;33mTo access via Ingress, add to /etc/hosts:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33m  127.0.0.1 hello.local\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\u001b[1;33mNote: Add '127.0.0.1 hello.local' to /etc/hosts to test Ingress\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33mThen run: curl -H 'Host: hello.local' http://localhost:8081\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[0;32m=== Demo Complete ===\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n  - Cluster created in 30-60 seconds\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Application deployed and accessible\r\n  - NodePort service configured\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Port-forwarding configured for easy access\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Ingress Controller installed and configured\r\n\r\nAccess points:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Port-forward (Service): http://localhost:8080\r\n  - Port-forward (Ingress): http://localhost:8081\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Direct node access: http://172.18.0.2:30759\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Ingress: http://hello.local (requires /etc/hosts entry: 127.0.0.1 hello.local)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "Important notes:\r\n  - Port-forward processes are running in background\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Service port-forward PID: 98134\r\n  - Ingress port-forward PID: 98432\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Stop port-forwards with: pkill -f 'kubectl port-forward'\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  - Or they will be stopped automatically when script exits\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "To clean up, run:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  pkill -f 'kubectl port-forward'  # Stop port-forwards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  kind delete cluster --name demo-cluster  # Delete cluster\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1;33mCleaning up port-forward processes (if running)...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
